<header class="hl-nav">
  <button class="hl-nav__menu" type="button" aria-controls="hl-drawer" aria-expanded="false" aria-label="Open menu">
    <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><line x1="3" y1="6" x2="21" y2="6"/><line x1="3" y1="12" x2="21" y2="12"/><line x1="3" y1="18" x2="21" y2="18"/></svg>
  </button>
  <a class="hl-nav__brand" href="{{ '/' | relative_url }}">
    <svg class="hl-brand__icon" viewBox="0 0 64 64" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><rect width="64" height="64" rx="14" fill="#161b22"/><rect x="1" y="1" width="62" height="62" rx="13" fill="none" stroke="#30363d" stroke-width="1.5"/><g stroke="#58a6ff" stroke-width="4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" fill="none"><path d="M19 16 V48 M35 16 V48 M19 32 H35"/><path d="M35 48 H50"/></g></svg>
    <span class="hl-brand__rule" aria-hidden="true"></span>
    <span class="hl-brand__stack">
      <span class="hl-brand__top">THE HUNTER&#8217;S</span>
      <span class="hl-brand__main">LEDGER<span class="hl-brand__dot" aria-hidden="true"></span></span>
    </span>
  </a>
  {%- comment -%} A plain GET form posting ?q= to /search/, which reads the parameter and
    runs the query, so the bar itself loads no search script. The magnifier is a <label>
    for the input: on phones the field collapses to the icon and clicking it focuses
    (and so expands) the field. Enter submits. {%- endcomment -%}
  <form class="hl-nav__search" action="{{ '/search/' | relative_url }}" method="get" role="search" aria-label="Search the site">
    <label class="hl-nav__search-icon" for="hl-nav-q" title="Search the Ledger">
      <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="7"/><line x1="21" y1="21" x2="16.65" y2="16.65"/></svg>
    </label>
    <input class="hl-nav__search-input" id="hl-nav-q" name="q" type="search" placeholder="Search the Ledger" aria-label="Search the site" autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false">
  </form>
</header>
{%- comment -%}
  Site navigation lives in a drawer that slides in from the left (assets/js/nav-drawer.js).
  The primary group is driven by `position:` front matter exactly as the old bar was, so
  adding a section is still one key on its page. The second group is the set of pages the
  footer also carries. Links are real anchors in the HTML whether or not the drawer is open,
  so crawlers and a reader without JavaScript (the footer repeats them) lose nothing.
{%- endcomment -%}
<div class="hl-drawer__backdrop" id="hl-drawer-backdrop" hidden></div>
<nav class="hl-drawer" id="hl-drawer" aria-label="Site navigation" aria-hidden="true" hidden>
  <div class="hl-drawer__head">
    <span class="hl-drawer__title">Menu</span>
    <button class="hl-drawer__close" type="button" aria-label="Close menu">
      <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><line x1="5" y1="5" x2="19" y2="19"/><line x1="19" y1="5" x2="5" y2="19"/></svg>
    </button>
  </div>
  <div class="hl-drawer__group">
    <div class="hl-drawer__label">Explore</div>
    {%- assign nav_pages = site.pages | where_exp: "item", "item.position" | sort: 'position' -%}
    {%- for nav_page in nav_pages -%}
      {%- unless nav_page.title == null or nav_page.hide or nav_page.title == site.title -%}
    <a class="hl-drawer__link" href="{{ nav_page.url | relative_url }}"{% if page.url == nav_page.url %} aria-current="page"{% endif %}>{{ nav_page.nav_title | default: nav_page.title }}</a>
      {%- endunless -%}
    {%- endfor -%}
  </div>
  <div class="hl-drawer__group">
    <div class="hl-drawer__label">More</div>
    <a class="hl-drawer__link" href="{{ '/search/' | relative_url }}"{% if page.url == '/search/' %} aria-current="page"{% endif %}>Search</a>
    <a class="hl-drawer__link" href="{{ '/consulting/' | relative_url }}"{% if page.url == '/consulting/' %} aria-current="page"{% endif %}>Consulting &amp; Advisory</a>
    <a class="hl-drawer__link" href="{{ '/sponsor/' | relative_url }}"{% if page.url == '/sponsor/' %} aria-current="page"{% endif %}>Sponsorship</a>
    <a class="hl-drawer__link" href="{{ '/about-me/' | relative_url }}"{% if page.url == '/about-me/' %} aria-current="page"{% endif %}>About Me</a>
    <a class="hl-drawer__link" href="{{ '/behind-the-reports/' | relative_url }}"{% if page.url == '/behind-the-reports/' %} aria-current="page"{% endif %}>Behind the Reports</a>
    <a class="hl-drawer__link" href="{{ '/pgp/' | relative_url }}"{% if page.url == '/pgp/' %} aria-current="page"{% endif %}>PGP Key</a>
    <a class="hl-drawer__link" href="{{ '/feed.xml' | relative_url }}">RSS Feed</a>
  </div>
</nav>
<script defer src="{{ '/assets/js/nav-drawer.js' | relative_url }}?v=1"></script>
